  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2)-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(3x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2))\\,-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(3x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x-2}-(-\\frac{1}{(3x-2)\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}}})\\cdot (3x-2)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x-2}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{(3x-2)\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x-2}(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\,1-(3x-2)^{2}\\,}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
